{"abstract":"As whole genome sequence data of microorganisms are becoming easily accessible and cheap to produce, a transformation of the traditional methods used for typing, phenotyping and phylogenetic analysis of microorganisms is on the way. Following the anticipation that most clinical microbiological and food safety laboratories will soon have a sequencer in use on a daily basis, there is a growing need for easy-to-use bioinformatics methods that can quickly convert the sequence data into useful information on, e.g., the type of bacteria, whether it is resistant towards any types of antibiotics, and whether it is part of an outbreak. The Center for Genomic Epidemiology, which is located at the Technical University of Denmark, has since its beginning in 2010 developed such bioinformatics methods and made them freely available as web-services. These web-services and their use is the focus of this chapter.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Larsen, Mette Voldby","Joensen, Katrine Grimstrup","Zankari, Ea","Ahrenfeldt, Johanne","Lukjancenko, Oksana","Kaas, Rolf Sommer","Roer, Louise","Leekitcharoenphon, Pimlapas","Saputra, Dhany","Cosentino, S.","Thomsen, Martin Christen Frølund","Bellod Cisneros, Jose Luis","Jurtz, Vanessa Isabell","Rasmussen, Simon","Petersen, Thomas Nordahl","Hasman, Henrik","Sicheritz-Pontén, Thomas","Aarestrup, Frank Møller","Lund, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-344515"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The University of Osaka"],"keyword":["Applied microbiology","Bioinformatics","Food Microbiology","Food Science","Life Sciences","Microbial Genetics and Genomics","Web services","Whole genome sequencing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the cge tool box","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-344515","ids":["dtu-85c970e4-bd27-4fa5-ad69-a096d3c55632"],"keyword":["Applied Microbiology","Bioinformatics","Food Microbiology","Food Science","Life Sciences","Microbial Genetics and Genomics","Web-services","Whole genome sequencing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-562FB0582FB3482CD76F428D4A8FB32E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Bio and Health Informatics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"jp","key":"the university of osaka","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"The University of Osaka","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Voldby","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"48f90aec-1c95-444e-a7e5-d7b3ddcf1b7e","name":"Larsen, Mette Voldby","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Grimstrup","key":"joensenpau","last":"Joensen","name":"Joensen, Katrine Grimstrup","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ea","key":"zankaripau","last":"Zankari","locid":"11bde48b-fac1-